From ccad100b37c43022e5b3dfde0fab49ac24bafdc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:14:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 062/206] feat(shorebird): IndirectStaticCallInstr -- the IL
 instruction, minus its pass

The other half of DD core. Where StaticCallInstr branches straight to its
target, this loads Thread::indirect_static_call_table_, indexes it by
dd_slot, and calls through the entry -- so a patch can repoint the target
while the call site stays put.

Shape is StaticCallInstr on the same TemplateDartCall<0> base with
ic_data_ and call_count_ dropped, which is why their function_ sits at
0xc0 where upstream's is at 0xd0. FIELD_LIST order is the serializer
order read off their WriteTo: function_, dd_slot_, result_type_, and the
32-bit field at 0xd8.

That last field is named shorebird_flags_ and deliberately given no
meaning. It is not a renamed upstream field: dropping the two makes 0xd8
land on upstream's is_known_list_constructor_ / entry_kind_ / identity_
span and all three are excluded -- a bool would be ldrb not ldr w,
entry_kind_ is contradicted by EmitNativeCode passing a hardcoded 0, and
AliasIdentity wraps an intptr_t so it is 8 bytes. The name says where it
lives and nothing about what it does.

Three decisions that are judgements rather than transcription:

  ConstantPropagator returns non_constant_. That is the correct answer,
  not a conservative one -- folding would bake in the pre-patch target and
  silently defeat the mechanism.

  ComputeType does not sharpen from the target's body, for the same
  reason: anything inferred from the pre-patch target is a claim about
  code that may not run.

  The Thread field is appended and reached through
  indirect_static_call_table_offset(). Their 0x978 is unusable here --
  their Shorebird block is mid-Thread, ours is appended, and hardcoding it
  would read an unrelated field while looking like a table-contents bug.

PrintOperandsTo reproduces their format string byte for byte, including
that theirs ends at the `]` and emits the argument separator only when
arguments follow, where upstream's format carries a trailing space.

VERIFICATION: ninja exit 0 (Release and Product); 76 of 77 shorebird tests
exit 0, the odd one being upstream's IsolateReload_ShapeChange_Const_AddSlot
which needs --dfe and passes with it; verify_reproduction.sh 24 artifacts
plus 14 stubs, 0 failures -- so adding an entry to FOR_EACH_INSTRUCTION and
a field to Thread moved neither the class table nor any dump.

NOT VERIFIED, and this is the honest gap: nothing constructs one of these
yet. The IL pass that rewrites static calls into indirect ones is fully
inlined in their binary and leaves zero symbols, so it has to be written
from scratch. Until then the class compiles and is regression-clean but is
not exercised by any test -- the AllocateMetadata() failure mode. A unit
test driving the constructor and PrintOperandsTo against their format
string is the next commit, before the pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/constant_propagator.cc b/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/constant_propagator.cc
